{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe rain here has been a veritable deluge, soaking the city from Sunday into today. Yet I insisted on the carriage to the Augarten, and thence to Nussdorf, for a mind that sits still too long grows rust. The air is thick, but the walk was good.\n\nLook at the enclosed petals. I stopped by a great pear tree on the road; the fruit was picked days ago, yet there it was, in full blossom again. It struck me as a strange defiance of the order of things, as if the tree had forgotten its own history. I picked two for you.\n\nI dined at a small inn in Nussdorf. The wine was ordinary, the bread hard, but the company—two young men from the University—was lively. They spoke of the new laws with a certainty that borders on arrogance, but one has to listen to see where the spirit is turning.\n\nTell the boys the rain does not stop the world, only the lazy. I am tired, but content.\n\nYour loving,\nG.W.F."}}],"created":1795219365,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":226,"prompt_tokens":1113,"total_tokens":1339,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-VIxM2TuLw7e2Vi4FxpwVDuplqVDqpCWB","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":1113,"prompt_ms":1055.15,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9480233602875113,"prompt_per_second":1054.8263280102353,"predicted_n":226,"predicted_ms":5344.455,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.753133333333334,"predicted_per_second":42.09970895067879}}